# Fixed 2026-09-30, defect 130's class, lane recovery-b4 (panel 183 R1,
# ratified 2026-09-30; the ffi-pragmatist's prediction). Symptom: design.md §4.19's
# own sqlite group with `sqlite3_open`'s `)` left out and one `)` too many on
# `sqlite3_close` drew one message, `expected_params_close` at the end of the
# first signature, and the stray `)` went unsaid until it was fixed: two
# turns. The next member's `function` before a name ends the reach at the
# member's margin, so the opener is named and the stray `)` is told, both in
# one `check`.

extern "sqlite3.h" link "sqlite3"
    constant SQLITE_OK: i64
    record Db tag sqlite3
    function sqlite3_open(path: cstr lent, @out: Db acquires sqlite3_close -> i64  #~ unclosed_bracket
    function sqlite3_close(db: Db consumes)) -> i64  #~ expected_extern_signature

function main()
    print(1)
